\subsection*{Preferential Attachment}
% preferential attachmentは、被引用数の分布において、すでに人気のある論文がより多くの被引用を集める傾向を指す。
Preferential attachment refers to the tendency for an already popular network node to attract more links from other nodes.
% 特に、ジャーナルでは、次の単位時間に得る被引用数は、すでに持っている被引用数と線形関係にあることが知られている。
Particularly in the journal article citation network, the number of citations gained in the next time unit is known to be linear to the number of citations already held\cite{JeongEtAl_MeasuringPreferentialAttachment_2003}.
% preferential attachment の強さは、それぞれの被引用数をもつ論文が次の単位時間に引用される確率 $\pi$ によって求められる。図~\ref{fig:pref_attch}には、累積の確率分布$\Pi = \int\pi dc $を示した。
Consider a probability $\Pi$ of a paper with a given citation count $c$ being cited in the next time unit.
The strength of preferential attachment is quantified by the exponent $\alpha$ in the following equation:
%Preferential attachment tells us that the 
\begin{align}
  \Pi(c) = \frac{c^\alpha}{\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i^\alpha}
\end{align}

In Figure~\ref{fig:pref_attch}.a, we show the cumulative probability distribution $\pi$ for better visibility.
The slope of the fitted line of the plot corresponds to the exponent $\alpha$.
\begin{align}
  \pi(c) = \int_{0}^{c}\Pi(c) dc 
\end{align}
where $\alpha > 1$ indicates a superlinear relationship, which would yield a more highly skewed distribution than with lower $\alpha$.

