However, it may happen that two vectors coincide. There are ${5 \choose 2}\cdot 3!=60$ combinatorial possibilities for that to happen. Any pair may coincide and the remaining points can be ordered in $3!$ possible ways. We will call such a situation {\it singly degenerate}.  The singly degenerate pentagon linkages of the same type topologically form an open segment within~$\mathcal{P}$, since one degree of freedom is needed to keep the two vectors aligned.
Every non-degenerate situation is surrounded by 5 possible singly degenerate situations since every pair of adjacent vectors may become coincident.


