Figure \ref{fig:maps2} shows the regular pentagon and a halo of its immediate neighborhood. It is worth contemplating a bit on this image. The geometric position of the shown pentagon linkages is chosen in a way that relates to their position in the corresponding tiling. The big black circular arcs in the background are hyperbolic lines consisting of the edges of the hyperbolic $(5,4)$-tiling. The interior points of those edges correspond to the singly degenerate situations.
Along each such line one pair of edges of the linkage points into the same direction. At places
where two such lines intersect (the vertices of the $(5,4)$-tiling)  {\it two} pairs of edges point in the same direction.
