The results above suggest that autocorrelation-driven effects (trend-following benefits or mean-reverting losses) might be weaker in markets where volatility clustering is strong. While our findings hold under AR(1)-GARCH(1,1) dynamics, future work could explore alternative specifications, such as regime-switching or rough volatility models, to further validate the generality of our results.

