\section{Conclusion}\label{section:F}
This paper presents an adaptive MPC approach with a variable prediction horizon to address transmission uncertainties for vehicle platoon system under non-ideal communication. The method employs tailored compensation packets for each vehicle and adjusts weighting matrices based on state deviations to balance response speed and tracking accuracy. Moreover, a prediction horizon update strategy is introduced to reduce computational complexity. Sufficient conditions for recursive feasibility and closed-loop stability are established. Simulation results demonstrate that the proposed approach significantly reduces computational requirements and computation time while maintaining system performance.


