    The main goal of the paper was to provide a proof-of-concept implementation of a general software tool for facilitating the operation of Virtual Laboratories that seamlessly combine the digital and physical world and enable AI-assisted research. We explained why previous attempts, ranging from purely virtual education environments and completely automated robot scientists to workflow managers and LLM-driven research loops, are insufficient for supporting the domain-agnostic digitalization of scientific research. We then characterized a potential software tool that resolves some of the open aspects.
