where $\cal D_{\rm test}$ is the test dataset,  $\#{\cal D_{\rm test}}$ is its size, and $ \alpha^*$ denotes the flux computed with one of the three methods. In Table \ref{tab:test_compar}, we highlight that the flux reconstruction is much more accurate, using both types of errors, when the VOFML method is used. In particular, when considering the MSE metric, VOFML is 43.7 times more accurate than UW and 13.2 times more accurate than LD, whereas when the MAE metric is involved, VOFML is 8.57 times more accurate than UW and 3.70 times more accurate than LD. Such an error is propagated at each time step during the simulation, it is thus crucial to reconstruct the flux in the most accurate way possible.

