\subsubsection{Dynamical Evolution}
We analyzed the dynamic evolution of the system using Equation (\ref{15}) until the second central moment, setting the diffusion parameters to zero. The error is then calculated using Equation (\ref{20}) by comparing the moment approach with the stochastic simulations.  

The results of this analysis are shown in Figure \ref{fig.1}. These figures show that the error everywhere is minimal. As the system size $\Omega$ increases, the error further decreases. Over time, the error diminishes but never reaches zero because of fluctuations that alter the dynamics and prevent the system from attaining a stationary state. Nevertheless, applying the second-moment approach to systems with second-order reactions provides a good approximation, because the error remains small.

