\subsection{Summary}
\label{sec44}

We have presented SSM results for NTME in Figs. \ref{fig3}, \ref{fig4} and \ref{fig5}. These results are compared with the results from other nuclear structure models in Fig. \ref{fig6}. As it is well known,  results from QRPA, EDF and IBM-2 are in general larger than SM results. As seen from the figure, results from the present statistical method (SSM) are within a factor of 2 compared to the shell model results. 
This shows that the results from SSM might improve further if one is able to relax some of the approximations used in Section III.

